# C4 review round 1 findings (reviewers: Kimi, agy, and the coordinator). Fix them on this branch.

The branch now also contains a merge of origin/wip/spec-core and a regenerated scripts/proofs/axioms.golden (HEAD 80b23d59, all seven gates pass on concrete-ci-2). Do not edit axioms.golden; the reviewer regenerates it. All rules of _review/BRIEF.md still apply (commit each piece after `nix develop -c timeout 1200 lake build ConcreteSpec` passes; do not push).

1. (major, Kimi+agy) Well-formedness preservation exists only for alloc. Prove `empty_wellFormed`, a geometry-preserving `modify` helper, `store_wellFormed`, `free_wellFormed`, `expose_wellFormed`, and in Proofs/Hybrid.lean preservation through `State.write`, `State.rawWrite`, `State.materialize`, `State.expose` (state a `State.WellFormed` that includes the memory invariant and that every materialized cell's range is a block of the right extent, if needed).
2. (major, Kimi+agy) The first-materialization law is missing: prove that if `st.read tgt p = some v` and `st.materialize tgt p ... = some (r, st')` (memory well-formed) then `st'.read tgt p = some v`; prove frame laws: `write`, `materialize`, `expose` leave `read` of every other place `q ≠ p` unchanged, provided q's materialized range (if any) is disjoint from p's (state the disjointness precisely). Add an integer materialize-then-read example.
3. (minor, agy) Add laws for `Memory.expose` (characterize success: the block is marked exposed, nothing else changes) and the completeness direction of `fromExposed`: if an eligible candidate contains the address then the result's provenance is that block (use candidate_contains_unique); if none contains it and some candidate's one-past equals the address, the result has provenance; if neither, `prov = none`. Do not add any tie-break the decided rule (Q3.9) does not have; if one-past candidates can tie, say so and list it under QUESTIONS instead of choosing.
4. (major, Kimi) `Ptr.addr` is an unrestricted Nat: on a target with 8-bit addresses, address 256 passes a zero-byte access, and encodePtr truncates it while decodePtr restores it from fragment metadata. Introduce target-relative pointer validity (address below 2^addrBits, space among the target's spaces), require it where accesses and encodings need it (zero-byte access included), and state decodePtr_encodePtr under it. Do not change decodePtr's behaviour on non-whole-pointer bytes (open owner question).
5. (major, Kimi) `Memory.Fits` does not check that the block's space is one of `tgt.spaces`; require it in Fits and in WellFormed.
